    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0706" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg618"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Scruggs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-08-30"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 278.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon the receipt of your telegram of the
                    22d instant, asking that a vessel of the U. S. Navy be dispatched forthwith to
                    La Guayra, I communicated copy thereof to the Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <p>Pending arrangments to dispatch a vessel, the arrival of the mail steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caracas</hi> on the 26th brought dispatches from your
                    legation and our consuls throwing light upon the urgency of your request.</p>
                <p>In regard to the reported taking of six passengers from the steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caracas</hi>, at Puerto Cabello, by order of Gen.
                    Urdaneta, the Department awaits full particulars of the occurrence before giving
                    you positive instructions.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
